MyShowcase System for MyBB 1.9
===============================

What it is
----------
MyShowcase is a plugin for MyBB 1.9. It turns a board into showcases: collections of entries with their own custom fields
(text, numbers, dates, choices and files), with comments, attachments, moderation, search, import and export of entries
as XML, and a web app manifest and service worker for each showcase.

Requirements
------------
- MyBB 1.9. The plugin is declared compatible with MyBB 1.9 (19*). MyBB 1.9 already ships Twig and several Symfony
  packages, and the plugin uses those copies.
- PHP 8.2 or higher, the version the plugin needs. MyBB 1.9's own PHP requirements also apply.
- A database engine that MyBB 1.9 supports: MySQL or MariaDB, PostgreSQL, or SQLite. The plugin creates its tables with
  the SQL of the engine your board runs on, when you activate it.
- PluginLibrary 13 or higher, installed at <mybb_root>/inc/plugins/pluginlibrary.php.
- Composer, to install the packages that MyBB 1.9 does not ship (symfony/form, symfony/dependency-injection and what they
  need; see step 3 below). If Composer is not available on your server, run it on your own computer and upload the
  resulting vendor folder.

Installation
------------
1. Back up your database and your MyBB files.
2. Copy the files and folders of the Upload folder of this repository into your MyBB root (not its CLAUDE.md, which is
   a note for developers), so that these paths exist:
   - <mybb_root>/inc/plugins/myshowcase.php (the plugin file)
   - <mybb_root>/inc/plugins/myshowcase/ (the plugin's code, its composer.json and its templates)
   - <mybb_root>/inc/tasks/myshowcase.php (the scheduled task)
   - <mybb_root>/inc/languages/ (the language files)
   - <mybb_root>/admin/modules/myshowcase/ (the admin pages)
   - <mybb_root>/showcase.php (the forum entry point of the showcases)
   - <mybb_root>/jscripts/ and <mybb_root>/images/ (scripts and images)
3. Install the plugin's Composer packages once, and again after each upgrade:

       cd <mybb_root>/inc/plugins/myshowcase
       composer install

   This creates <mybb_root>/inc/plugins/myshowcase/vendor/.
4. In the Admin CP, go to Configuration > Plugins and choose Activate & Install for MyShowcase System.
5. In the Admin CP, go to Users and Groups > Admin Permissions, select the administrators who should manage the
   MyShowcase System, open the MyShowcase tab and grant the permissions you want.
6. Open MyShowcase Admin > Help Page for the detailed instructions.

Every user group starts with the default permissions listed in Documentation/permissions.md. Change a group's permissions
on its MyShowcase tab (Users and Groups > Usergroups) only where you want something other than the default.

Documentation
-------------
The documentation is in the Documentation folder of this repository:

- Documentation/README.txt: installation and upgrade notes, the settings of a showcase, and the change log.
- Documentation/permissions.md: the default permissions of the user groups.
- Documentation/import.md, Documentation/import-packages.md and Documentation/exports.md: importing and exporting entries.
- Documentation/visibility.md: who may see which entries, comments and attachments.
- Documentation/showcases/: the settings of a showcase, such as the URL option.
- Documentation/templates/template-reference.md: the templates of the plugin.
- Documentation/schema/: planned changes to the database schema.
- Documentation/pending-work.md: open items for the maintainers.
- Documentation/history/LANGUAGE_REFACTORING_SUMMARY.md: the change of the language keys from camelCase to snake_case,
  kept for reference.
